<title>USA: TABLE - WorldCom Q2 profit vs proforma loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - WorldCom Q2 profit vs proforma loss.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSON, Miss. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second quarter</p>
<p>				1997		  1996 (proforma)</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	  $0.08     loss	 $0.09</p>
<p> Shr	profit	   0.08     loss	  0.52</p>
<p> Net	profit	   72.0     loss	 444.9</p>
<p> Revs		     1,770.1		  1,334.4</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   895.5		    391.2</p>
<p>Year-to-date</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	  $0.13     loss	 $0.19</p>
<p> Shr	profit	   0.13     loss	  0.62</p>
<p> Net	profit	  115.1     loss	 526.8</p>
<p> Revs		     3,447.3		  2,578.2</p>
<p> Avg			  891.9		    389.4</p>
<p>(All data above in millions except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: WordCom Inc's 1996 figures are pro-forma to compare year-over-year growth.</p>
<p>The company took non-cash charges and had extraordinary items in the second quarter and first half of 1996.</p>
<p>Using actual figures, the company posted a $268.0 million loss, or $0.69 a share loss, in the 1996 quarter. Operating income before the non-cash charges and extraordinary items was $0.25 a share profit in the 1996 quarter.</p>
<p>For the six months in 1996, the company had an actual net loss of $182.2 million, or $0.46 loss a share. Operating income before the non-cash charges and extraordinary items was a profit of $0.46 a share.</p>
</text>
